- No model/dataset access; assume open-weights target models (e.g., Llama-3-8B-Instruct, Mistral-7B-Instruct, Vicuna-7B/13B, Gemma-2-9B-it) and open attacker models; judge = Llama-Guard-3-8B plus a GPT-4-class judge if possible.
- Execution is impossible and not required: no network, no GPU, no ML libraries in the environment; deliverable is a design document only.
- Compute budget unknown → present a parameterized budget and a reduced pilot-sampling plan (e.g., stratified sampling of 100 behaviors per dataset).
- "Previously tested tricks" is ambiguous — two operationalizations (history-in-context vs population seeding); researcher confirmation against the source needed.

